<MainLayout>

  <section class="hero">

    <h1>Contact & Licensing Inquiries</h1>

    <p>
      Dual Brain Robotics welcomes inquiries regarding research,
      collaboration, licensing, investment, media coverage,
      and strategic partnerships.
    </p>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Licensing Opportunities</h2>

    <p>
      Organizations interested in licensing, developing,
      evaluating, or commercializing aspects of the
      Dual Brain Robotics Architecture are invited
      to make contact.
    </p>

    <p>
      Particular areas of interest include:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Robotics</li>
      <li>Artificial Intelligence</li>
      <li>Cognitive Architectures</li>
      <li>Human-Robot Interaction</li>
      <li>Assistive Technologies</li>
      <li>Research Partnerships</li>
    </ul>

  </section>

  <section class="section">

    <h2>Research & Media</h2>

    <p>
      Researchers, journalists, podcast hosts, and
      conference organizers are welcome to inquire
      regarding interviews, presentations, and
      discussions of the Dual Brain Robotics project.
    </p>

  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <h2>Contact</h2>
<p>
For licensing, partnership, research, media, or investment inquiries:
</p>
<p>Alexander Durig, Ph.D.</p>
<p>alex@dualbrainrobotics.com</p>
<p>Founder, Dual Brain Robotics</p>

  </section>

</MainLayout>
